    },
    "message": "Read an inserted container again before writing to it, and lint for it\n\nThe Rust port keeps model_state in tracked containers that convert a plain\ncontainer on insert, so a write through the name it had before the insert would\nreach neither the tree nor Rust. Three sites did that. Results and the 674\nCheckpoint files of the seven-day run stay byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
